  "id": "Compound::DB00589 - Gene::1815",
  "verbalization": "Lisuride is implicated in the pathogenesis of both Erythromelalgia and Pleural Fibrosis, which are both associated with Bromocriptine. These conditions are linked to Drd4 through a common mechanism: Bromocriptine binds to Drd4. The evidence suggests that Lisuride may exert its effects via a pathway that involves Bromocriptine, which in turn interacts with Drd4. The lowest common ancestors of Lisuride and Bromocriptine are both classified as Organonitrogen Compounds and Agents Affecting the Nervous System, indicating a shared pharmacological profile. This integrated pathway implies that Lisuride may modulate Drd4 through a bromocriptine-mediated mechanism, potentially influencing downstream signaling pathways. The evidence supports a relationship between Lisuride and Drd4, mediated by Bromocriptine, highlighting a possible role in neurochemical regulation.",
